cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software when using the workstation, and cite the original methods and datasets selected in your research plan."
type: software
title: "YeastVar1011: evidence-linked study design and quality control for yeast single-cell research"
authors:
  - family-names: Dong
    given-names: Yue
version: 22.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-09
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23429611
    description: "Concept DOI for all versions"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/YueDong0211/YeastVar1011"
url: "https://yuedong0211.github.io/YeastVar1011/"
abstract: "A browser-based workstation that connects yeast single-cell study questions to source-attributed marker evidence, analysis methods, input requirements and reproducible research plans. A separate Linux Snakemake workflow performs raw-read quality control and STARsolo counting for explicitly configured fixed CB/UMI layouts. The catalogue covers expression variation, RNA dynamics, regulation, population genetics and evolution."
keywords:
  - Saccharomyces cerevisiae
  - single-cell RNA sequencing
  - study design
  - marker evidence
  - quality control
  - expression variation
